<h2 id="method">How the cut was made</h2>
<p>Source ran 44.1 kHz and 24 bit stereo across 3.58 GB. The detector made one decode pass,
tracked pulse, split the tape into 83 takes, then scored each one on length, section
changes, pulse strength, continuity, ending shape, and tempo stability.</p>
<p>A take was proven aborted when a later take replayed its opening in the same pitch order.
Sequence order carries the evidence, since an average across pitches would match any two
songs sharing a key.</p>
<p>Every delivered file was then re-decoded from scratch and measured against the room noise
floor of -40.2 dB, so no file counts as verified on the strength of the same numbers that
selected it. Three files had leading dead air removed by hand after that check.</p>

